426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Showing only abstract idea and hiding the implementation is called Data Abstraction .)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (There are two ways to achieve data abstraction.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (1. Interfaces: It is a way to achieve 100% data abstraction, because all the method inside the interface are only declared not even a single method is defined.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. Abstract Class: It is a way to achieve the partial data abstraction because inside an abstract class some method are declared and some method are defined.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (NOTE : We cannot create object of interfaces and abstract class . )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
